I watched it again with my kids several years ago and I've seen scattered episodes again when my daughter Ella rewatched it.
几年前我和我的孩子们又看了一遍，当我女儿艾拉重看时，我又看到了零散的剧集。

00:50:10.489 --> 00:50:17.820
I was thrilled to hear an ad for William, how we made your mother a couple of weeks ago and then Crestfallen a couple days later.
我很高兴听到威廉的广告，几周前我们如何让你的母亲，几天后我们如何让你垂头丧气。

00:50:17.820 --> 00:50:20.946
When I found out I had missed over a season and a half.
当我发现我已经错过了一个半赛季的时候。

00:50:20.946 --> 00:50:21.855
I'm catching up.
我正在追赶。

00:50:21.855 --> 00:50:25.947
But I'm sad I missed my chances to participate in the discussion so far.
但我很遗憾到目前为止我错过了参与讨论的机会。

00:50:25.947 --> 00:50:26.969
It's not too late.
还不算太晚。

00:50:26.969 --> 00:50:27.725
It's not too late.
还不算太晚。

00:50:27.725 --> 00:50:28.229
Here we are.
我们到了。

00:50:28.229 --> 00:50:29.530
We're discussing you right now.
我们现在正在讨论你。

00:50:29.530 --> 00:50:43.901
By regret that having missed out is so great that I'm going to risk alienating myself and getting all subsequent emails trashed, unopened by using this first one to make a comment on your first few episodes through the Blue French Horn nay pilot episode.
遗憾的是，错过的机会是如此之大，以至于我将冒着疏远自己的风险，并通过使用第一封电子邮件对您通过蓝色法国号试播集的前几集发表评论，将所有后续电子邮件都扔掉，未打开。

00:50:43.901 --> 00:50:51.369
A good portion of those episodes talked about what made him different and why the viewers who called and wrote and loved it so much.
这些剧集的很大一部分讨论了他的与众不同之处，以及为什么打电话、写信并如此喜爱它的观众。

00:50:51.369 --> 00:50:57.119
I've recommended hymnium to many people over the years, and I always felt disappointed.
多年来我向很多人推荐了赞美诗，但我总是感到失望。

00:50:57.119 --> 00:51:03.840
It felt important to me to convey why it was so good, and that it was good in a different way from other sitcoms we would talk about.
对我来说，传达为什么它如此出色以及它与我们谈论的其他情景喜剧不同的方式很重要。

00:51:03.840 --> 00:51:08.579
I needed to get them to appreciate what was going on here, and I couldn't do it.
我需要让他们了解这里发生的事情，但我做不到。

00:51:08.579 --> 00:51:13.480
Listening to how we made your mother so far is a welcome opportunity to make a more informed go at it.
到目前为止，聆听我们如何塑造你的母亲是一个很好的机会，可以让你更了解这一点。

00:51:13.480 --> 00:51:20.000
Hymnium didn't teach me anything foundational, or get me through anything, or change the path of my life for the better.
Hymnium 没有教给我任何基础知识，也没有帮助我经历任何事情，也没有让我的人生道路变得更好。

00:51:20.000 --> 00:51:28.320
Yet, I still think I have as deep a love and connection to the show as those listeners who called or wrote and telling you how it did those things for them.
然而，我仍然认为我对这部剧有着深深的热爱和联系，就像那些打电话或写信告诉你它是如何为他们做这些事情的听众一样。

00:51:28.320 --> 00:51:30.840
Okay, almost as deep.
好吧，差不多一样深。

00:51:30.840 --> 00:51:40.320
Another clue to what makes the show so special is Matt Rice's reason for his immediate and unique reaction to him, him, among your new series ideas.
这部剧如此特别的另一个线索是马特·赖斯（Matt Rice）对你的新系列创意中的他，他的立即而独特的反应的原因。

00:51:40.320 --> 00:51:47.320
Another was the divided industry reaction as you shopped and started the show and the common threat of those who, quote, got it.
另一个原因是，当你购物并开始演出时，行业反应不一，以及那些得到它的人的共同威胁。

00:51:47.320 --> 00:51:59.639
And then there were your observations about the audacious vulnerability of Ted's character, which we see so well written and acted in that pilot speech after he fucks it up with Robin, and Craig admitting how he felt evil casting calamities in their path.
然后是你对泰德性格中大胆脆弱的观察，我们在他与罗宾搞砸后的试播演讲中看到了这一点，他在与罗宾搞砸后的演讲中看到了如此出色的写作和表演，克雷格也承认他对在他们的道路上制造灾难感到邪恶。

00:51:59.639 --> 00:52:08.880
Previously, I felt the closest I came to identifying what makes the show special is when I would tell people that the writers and the characters know it's all about the story.
以前，我觉得最接近确定这部剧的特别之处的时候是我告诉人们编剧和角色都知道这一切都与故事有关。

00:52:08.880 --> 00:52:17.434
This was something my friends and I had been saying through our 20s, it's for the story, from some ill-advised and quickly hopeless adventure I wish I could remember.
这是我和我的朋友在 20 多岁的时候一直在说的话，这是为了故事，来自一些不明智且很快绝望的冒险，我希望我能记住。

00:52:17.434 --> 00:52:21.402
Even after beefing it up into a folk philosophy, it was obviously inadequate.
即使将其强化为民间哲学之后，它显然还是不够的。

00:52:21.402 --> 00:52:25.164
After listening to how we made your mother, here's what I think I missed.
听完我们如何造就你的母亲后，我想我错过了以下几点。

00:52:25.164 --> 00:52:27.019
There are two kinds of storytelling.
讲故事有两种。

00:52:27.019 --> 00:52:28.404
One is to get something.
一是为了得到一些东西。

00:52:28.404 --> 00:52:30.999
Claps, laughs, ticket sales, ratings, clicks.
鼓掌、笑声、售票、收视率、点击。

00:52:30.999 --> 00:52:34.171
Something that always comes down to money or celebrity.
一些事情总是归结为金钱或名人。

00:52:34.171 --> 00:52:35.266
It's transactional.
这是交易性的。

00:52:35.266 --> 00:52:36.420
The other is caring.
另一个是关心。

00:52:36.420 --> 00:52:40.514
It's storytelling to people you care about as a way of caring for them.
这是向你关心的人讲故事，作为关心他们的一种方式。

00:52:40.514 --> 00:52:42.244
You're gifting them something.
你在送他们一些东西。

00:52:42.244 --> 00:52:48.300
Sometimes it's just respite, but usually and always if the story is nine years long, it's more than that.
有时这只是喘息的机会，但通常情况下，如果故事长达九年，那么它的意义就不止于此。

00:52:48.860 --> 00:52:53.820
Of course, the two can overlap, but for any given story, I think it's pretty clear which is primary.
当然，两者可以重叠，但对于任何给定的故事，我认为哪个是主要的是非常清楚的。

00:52:53.820 --> 00:52:59.900
I think him, Yum, was one of the rare sitcoms where caring storytelling was primary.
我认为他，百胜，是少有的以关爱故事讲述为主要内容的情景喜剧之一。

00:52:59.900 --> 00:53:01.155
Then what a generous comment.
那么这是多么慷慨的评论啊。

00:53:01.155 --> 00:53:03.579
I love that breakdown of, and you are trying to do both.
我喜欢这种崩溃，而你正试图两者兼得。

00:53:03.579 --> 00:53:04.758
We wanted to be a hit.
我们想成为热门。

00:53:04.758 --> 00:53:06.311
We wanted to stay on the air.
我们想继续直播。

00:53:06.311 --> 00:53:07.597
We wanted to stay alive.
我们想活下去。

00:53:07.597 --> 00:53:11.025
We had to think commercially, because that was them's the rules.
我们必须从商业角度思考，因为这就是他们的规则。

00:53:11.025 --> 00:53:17.880
But I do think the deeper and more primary thing was what resonates with humans, and if that came across that, that means a lot.
但我确实认为更深层、更主要的东西是与人类产生共鸣的东西，如果能够实现这一点，那就意义重大。

00:53:17.880 --> 00:53:19.327
Thank you for that message.
谢谢你的留言。

00:53:19.327 --> 00:53:20.612
That means an awful lot.
这意味着很多。

00:53:20.612 --> 00:53:22.380
That's what we were trying to do.
这就是我们试图做的。

00:53:22.380 --> 00:53:34.053
I mean, I think one thing you'll hear from the show, from Craig, from me and from other people who were deeply involved in the making of it, we did care.
我的意思是，我认为你会从这部剧中听到一件事，从克雷格、我和其他深度参与制作的人那里，我们确实很关心。

00:53:34.053 --> 00:53:38.860
We cared a lot, and I'm glad that That comes through, you know?
我们非常关心，我很高兴这一切得以实现，你知道吗？

00:53:38.860 --> 00:53:40.139
Yeah, me too.
是的，我也是。

00:53:40.139 --> 00:53:50.659
And that's, I think that's why we're still here talking about it, it's why we're all still friends, and that is the type of art we want to hopefully still be making, and that's the spirit of this very podcast.
这就是，我认为这就是为什么我们仍然在这里谈论它，这就是为什么我们仍然是朋友，这就是我们希望仍然能够制作的艺术类型，这就是这个播客的精神。

00:53:50.659 --> 00:54:00.219
Yeah, and I am, we are signing off in the spirit of great optimism that in an hour and 15 minutes, Craig Thomas and I will be having dinner together.
是的，我是，我们本着非常乐观的精神签署协议，一小时十五分钟后，克雷格·托马斯和我将一起吃晚饭。

00:54:00.219 --> 00:54:03.340
I think we'll now have talked about this dinner in like four or five episodes.
我想我们现在应该用四五集的时间来讨论这顿晚餐。

00:54:03.340 --> 00:54:04.980
This will like cover months.
这就像盖几个月一样。

00:54:04.980 --> 00:54:07.139
People will be hearing about this into the fall.
到秋天人们都会听到这个消息。

00:54:07.139 --> 00:54:09.139
We'll have to follow up and say how the dinner went after.
我们必须跟进并说明晚餐后的情况。

00:54:09.139 --> 00:54:09.980
I know, I know.
我知道，我知道。

00:54:09.980 --> 00:54:10.980
There's a lot of pressure.
压力很大。

00:54:10.980 --> 00:54:12.099
A post-mortem.
尸检。

00:54:12.099 --> 00:54:14.619
What if we sit across from each other and I'm just like, I got nothing?
如果我们坐在对面，而我却说，我什么都没有怎么办？

00:54:14.619 --> 00:54:19.820
I know, it's like we're talking all the time on a computer screen and we're just, it doesn't track carry over to real life.
我知道，这就像我们一直在电脑屏幕上交谈，但它并没有追踪到现实生活中的情况。

00:54:19.820 --> 00:54:20.659
I'd be like, you sure?
我会说，你确定吗？

00:54:20.659 --> 00:54:21.500
You're in person.
你是个人。

00:54:21.500 --> 00:54:29.940
We're, it has been a minute since I've actually seen you in person, which is fucking absurd because you're 20 minutes from me.
我们，自从我真正见到你本人以来已经有一分钟了，这太荒谬了，因为你离我只有 20 分钟的路程。

00:54:29.940 --> 00:54:31.340
Guess what, I'm coming your way.
你猜怎么着，我正朝你走来。

00:54:31.340 --> 00:54:33.420
I'm coming to Brooklyn, that's how much I love you.
我要来布鲁克林，这就是我有多爱你。

00:54:33.420 --> 00:54:34.260
Yeah.
是的。

00:54:34.260 --> 00:54:36.300
All right, everybody, we love you all too.
好吧，大家，我们也爱你们。

00:54:36.300 --> 00:54:37.300
See you soon.
再见。

00:54:37.300 --> 00:54:47.000
I am guilty, please equip me, all sins are forgiven, in New York City.
我有罪，请装备我，所有的罪孽都被宽恕，在纽约。

